	<key>readme</key>
	<string># Agenda

Your calendar in Alfred: what is next, the days ahead, a week and a month at a glance, and a prompt to join when a meeting starts.

## Keywords

* `cal`: the next meeting, then upcoming days. Type to search, `+` to add an event or `-` to delete one (below).
* `day`: one day with its free gaps. Add a day: `day tomorrow`, `day fri`, `day 24/11`.
* `week`: seven days as columns. `week +1` for next week.
* `month`: the month as a calendar. `month dec`, `month +1`.
* `join`: join the meeting that is on or about to start.

Every keyword can be changed in **Configure Workflow…**

## Keys

* &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; joins a meeting that is on or starts within 15 minutes; otherwise opens the event in Calendar.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; does the other of those two.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌥&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; copies the meeting link (or the event details).
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌃&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; shows that day.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;L&lt;/kbd&gt; shows the event details in Large Type; &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;C&lt;/kbd&gt; copies them.
* In the week and month grids: &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; opens the day, &lt;kbd&gt;⌥&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; goes forward, &lt;kbd&gt;⌃&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; goes back, &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; opens the day in Calendar. Typing filters the days by date or event name.
* On a **Free** row, &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; offers to block that time.

## Adding events

Type `+` after `cal`, then what and when: `cal + dentist tomorrow 15:00`, `cal + lunch fri 12-13`, `cal + review 24/11 14.00 for 30 min`, `cal + offsite mon` (a day alone makes an all-day event). Times are 24-hour unless they say am or pm, and an event lasts an hour unless you give a range or a length. The first row uses the calendar from **Configure Workflow…** (or your default calendar), the rows below offer the others, and `@exchange` or `@home` puts a calendar first. &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; adds the event.

## Deleting events

Type `-` after `cal`, then part of the event's name: `cal - dentist`. &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; on an event asks first: the top row, **Keep it**, goes back, and only the row below it deletes. A repeating event also offers to delete that one and every later one. Meetings with other people, invitations and events in read-only calendars can't be deleted here, because that would cancel or decline them for everyone: &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; opens them in Calendar instead.

## Meeting alerts

With **Meeting alerts** on, a small background job (a LaunchAgent named `com.situmorang.agenda.alerts`) checks once a minute and acts when a meeting is about to start. If your screen is locked then, you get a notification, and the join prompt (or the automatic join) waits until you unlock, up to 5 minutes after the start. Setting it to **Off** removes the job the next time you open the agenda.

## Calendar access

The calendar is read by `bin/agenda-calendar`, which holds its own *Full Calendar Access* permission (System Settings › Privacy &amp; Security › Calendars). Nothing leaves your Mac.

## Changing the code

Sources are in `src/`. Run `./build.sh` in the workflow folder to rebuild. Rebuilding `agenda-calendar` makes macOS ask for calendar access again; `build.sh` only does that when its source changed.
